  slide "Lane-salted seed" {
    eyebrow: "Lane-salted seed"
    title: "SHA-256 of base:trace:lane seeds NumPy PCG64"
    lede: "`seed_for_trace_lane` hashes `\"{base}:{trace_id}:{lane}\"` (SHA-256, first 8 bytes BE). Base is `t_star_random_seed` — decorrelated per trace and lane."

    narration: "Each open-window draw salts the dedicated t* random seed with the trace id and lane index. The salted string is hashed, and the digest becomes the per-lane RNG seed. Same seed and inputs always reproduce the same t*; different traces or lanes decorrelate."

    term: {
      word: "seed_for_trace_lane"
      meaning: "SHA-256(\"{base_seed}:{trace_id}:{lane}\") → first 8 bytes big-endian as the per-(trace, lane) NumPy PCG64 seed. Base is t_star_random_seed."
    }

    points: [
      "Formula: `SHA256(\"{base}:{trace_id}:{lane}\")` → low 8 bytes BE → `u64` seed.",
      "Base seed is config `t_star_random_seed` (not the run-root `random_seed`).",
      "Open draws use `NumpyPcg64::from_u64_seed(seed).uniform(lo, hi)`.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/tstar.rs` — `seed_for_trace_lane`."
    ]

    caption: "t_star_random_seed · salted per (trace, lane) · PCG64."

    render: @scene {
      roots: [
        {
          id: "s8-hdr"
          capability: "core.header"
