  slide "Trie chop" {
    eyebrow: "Trie chop"
    title: "Drop pre-t* nodes; re-root survivors from START"
    lede: "`chop_trie_at_tstar` drops `arrival_offset_us < t*`, then re-roots survivors that lost all predecessors from `START` with `min_start_delay_us = arrival − t*`."

    narration: "The snapshot chop removes every node whose arrival is strictly before t*. Survivors that still have a surviving predecessor keep their inter-turn edge. Survivors that lost all real predecessors get a synthetic start edge whose delay is the residual arrival minus t*. Edges between survivors stay as recorded."

    term: {
      word: "chop_trie_at_tstar"
      meaning: "Format-agnostic segment-trie chop: drop arrivals before t*, re-root orphan survivors from START at residual delay arrival − t*, leave prompt paths intact."
    }

    points: [
      "Drop nodes with `arrival_offset_us < t*` (motif: mute/remove `n0` · `n1`).",
      "Re-root orphans from `START` with `min_start_delay_us = arrival − t*`.",
      "`t* ≤ 0` returns the graph unchanged (full replay).",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/snapshot.rs` — `chop_trie_at_tstar`."
