  slide "Cache-pressure warmup" {
    eyebrow: "Cache-pressure warmup"
    title: "Extended warmup replays the post-t* remainder under pressure"
    lede: "Cache-pressure warmup is the extended phase: lanes recycle chopped post-`t*` graphs against the server so KV stays under load before the handoff drain."

    narration: "After the boundary chop, duration-bounded lanes repeatedly dispatch pressure templates — each plan is the post-t* remainder at that lane's salted t*. The goal is cache pressure: keep the inference server's KV busy with live frontier traffic until the clock deadline, then drain into the handoff."

