  slide "PermutationDraw" {
    eyebrow: "GraphPressureRecycle + PermutationDraw"
    title: "Sequential · Shuffle · Random — child seeds from run root"
    lede: "`PermutationDraw` remaps the shared corpus cursor: Sequential (`x % n`), Shuffle (persistent epoch), or Random (MT19937 choice). Shuffle/Random child seeds derive from run-root `random_seed` — not `t_star_random_seed`."

    narration: "Pressure and profiling share one strategy-aware corpus draw. Sequential walks the corpus in order. Shuffle uses a persistent without-replacement epoch. Random picks with replacement. Those child seeds come from the run-root random seed — explicitly not from the dedicated t* seed, which only salts per-lane t* draws."

    term: {
      word: "PermutationDraw"
      meaning: "Corpus-index remap: Sequential x%total; Shuffle persistent-epoch without replacement; Random with-replacement MT19937 choice. Shuffle/Random seeds via sampler_*_seed(run root)."
    }

    points: [
      "Modes: `Sequential` · `Shuffle` · `Random` (`GraphSamplingStrategy` / `RecycleDrawMode`).",
      "Shuffle child seed: `SHA256(\"{root}:dataset.sampler.shuffle\")` → NumPy PCG64 epochs.",
      "Random child seed: `SHA256(\"{root}:dataset.sampler.random\")` → Python MT19937 — root is `random_seed`, not `t_star_random_seed`.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/tstar.rs` — `sampler_shuffle_seed` / `sampler_random_seed`; `graph_input.rs` — `TStarWindow::recycle_draw`."
    ]

    caption: "t* uses t_star_random_seed · recycle uses run-root random_seed."

    render: @scene {
      roots: [
        {
          id: "s13-hdr"
          capability: "core.header"
