  slide "Drain & handoff" {
    eyebrow: "Drain & handoff"
    title: "LaneHandoff carries what the seed cannot replay"
    lede: "After every credit return lands, warmup stashes one `GraphWarmupHandoff`. Profiling consumes it once and resumes each live lane at its recorded frontier."

    narration: "The seeded t* plan is shared across phases, so the handoff only carries what determinism cannot reproduce: which template each lane was mid-flight on, which nodes actually executed, and when their returns landed. Deck-level fields stamp the drain wall, the next corpus cursor, and how many pressure lanes ran."

    term: {
      word: "LaneHandoff"
      meaning: "Per-lane drain state: template_trace_id, instance_id, t_star_us, executed_node_ids, return_wall_us — plus deck-level drain_end_wall_us, corpus_cursor, pressure_lane_count."
    }

    points: [
      "`LaneHandoff`: `template_trace_id`, `instance_id`, `t_star_us`, `executed_node_ids`, `return_wall_us`.",
      "`GraphWarmupHandoff`: `lanes`, `drain_end_wall_us`, `corpus_cursor`, `pressure_lane_count`.",
      "t* plan is not carried — both phases derive it from the seeded sampler.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/warmup_handoff.rs`; `graph_phase_runtime.rs` — `build_warmup_handoff`."
    ]

    caption: "Drain stamp · per-lane frontier · shared cursor."

