  slide "Profiling resume" {
    eyebrow: "Profiling resume"
    title: "Frontier chop · skip executed · residual from return walls"
    lede: "`chop_trie_at_frontier` drops pre-`t*` history and executed nodes, then re-roots survivors with residual delays from `return_wall_us` vs `drain_end_wall_us` (capped by `HANDOFF_RESIDUAL_CAP_SEC`)."

    narration: "For each handoff lane, profiling loads the original template, chops at the frontier with the executed set and return walls, and keeps the pressure instance id. Survivors that lost predecessors re-root from START; residual delay is derived from how long ago each predecessor returned relative to drain — not a fresh t* draw."

    term: {
      word: "chop_trie_at_frontier"
      meaning: "Resume chop: drop pre-t* and executed nodes; re-root survivors using residual delays from return walls and drain_end_wall_us; do not refire server-held KV."
    }

    points: [
      "Drop `arrival_offset_us < t*` and every id in `executed_node_ids`.",
      "Re-root residuals from `return_wall_us` vs `drain_end_wall_us` (cap 60s).",
      "Server already holds executed KV — profiling must not refire those nodes.",
      "Evidence: `snapshot.rs` — `chop_trie_at_frontier`; `graph_phase_runtime.rs` — `build_profiling_resume_lane_plans`."
    ]

