  slide "Abort / edge cases" {
    eyebrow: "Abort / edge cases"
    title: "Warmup abort · t*≤0 unchanged · collapsed [0,0] window"
    lede: "Terminal warmup failures abort before profiling. `chop_trie_at_tstar` with `t* ≤ 0` returns the graph unchanged. A collapsed window (`hi ≤ lo`, default `[0,0]`) yields an exact no-draw instant."

    narration: "Warmup trace failures populate a run-scoped ledger; after drain the run aborts with trajectory_warmup_failed rather than profiling on a corrupt frontier. A non-positive t* skips the topology chop entirely — full replay. The default zero window collapses to t*=0 without drawing RNG."

